      ],
      "source": "https://www.rheaheraldnews.com/lifestyles/article_3c4a6a90-5067-4d32-8380-c3cf37e10be6.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town\u2019s post office opened in 1878, with Gray himself serving as the second postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rheaheraldnews.com/lifestyles/article_3c4a6a90-5067-4d32-8380-c3cf37e10be6.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Graysville\u2019s growth began when the Cincinnati Southern Railroad arrived in 1880, drawing new settlers to the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rheaheraldnews.com/lifestyles/article_3c4a6a90-5067-4d32-8380-c3cf37e10be6.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Graysville rests 1,140 feet above sea level, giving it a modest hilltop setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
